            <ArticleTitle>Traumatic thrombosis of the left main coronary artery and myocardial infarction caused by blunt chest trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>672-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 38-year-old man who, after a blunt chest trauma, developed an acute transmural myocardial infarction. Coronary arteriography revealed a thrombus in the left main artery, occlusion of the distal left anterior descending artery, and a diagonal branch caused by emboli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
